@node CMacs Transcode
@chapter CMacs Transcode: Native ffmpeg Batch Transcoder

@cindex transcode
@cindex ffmpeg
@cindex compress_video
@cindex compress_audio
@cindex podman
@cindex linuxserver/ffmpeg

@code{cmacs-transcode} is a native reimplementation of the author's
@command{compress_video} and @command{compress_audio} shell scripts: it
batch-transcodes video and audio with ffmpeg, driven entirely from inside
Emacs.  Emacs itself spawns and supervises the ffmpeg processes as a bounded
parallel pool (no GNU parallel), and streams live per-job status into a
dedicated queue buffer that redraws on a timer.

By default it runs ffmpeg inside a podman or docker
@code{linuxserver/ffmpeg} container --- which is guaranteed to carry a full
codec set that a stock host ffmpeg may lack --- and transparently falls back
to a host @command{ffmpeg} binary when no container runtime is present.

It is a pure-Elisp subsystem (no C).  Enable it with
@option{--with-cmacs-transcode} (part of the standard flag set); at runtime
it needs podman, docker, or a host @command{ffmpeg}.  The build flag is
exposed as @code{IS-CMACS-TRANSCODE} and @code{(cmacs-feature-p 'transcode)}.

